```c
static inline struct sk_buff *skb_share_check(struct sk_buff *skb, gfp_t pri)
{
	might_sleep_if(gfpflags_allow_blocking(pri));
	if (skb_shared(skb)) {
		struct sk_buff *nskb = skb_clone(skb, pri);
		if (likely(nskb))
			__kfree_skb(skb);
		else
			skb = NULL;
		skb = nskb;
	}
	return skb;
}
```

skb_clone shares the same head data, so pointers into data remain valid. Not a head realloc. So skb_share_check candidates are lower priority.

